Meeting goal: Discuss signature status in DdS.

Wednesday, 26.11.2025, online meeting, 9:30-10:00
Participants: Mélanie, João, Tomás, Manuel, Chris, Karin, Xiaojin


	• Problem: Greengrocer contract with SERI needs to be signed; and Xiaojin has signed contracts since she started.
	• Karin does not want to sign Greengrocer contract together with Chris because of institutional conflicts => need of another board member to sign.
	• Current status:
		○ Statutes say that all contracts need to be signed by two. Note that the english translation (which is legally not binding) says something differen "at least two":
			§ "11. Zeichnungsberechtigung. Der Vorstand regelt die Zeichnungsberechtigung zu zweien."
			§ "11. Authority to sign. At least two members of the Board of Directors must sign any legal instrument on behalf of the Association."  --> Eventually change this version to be compliant with the german version.
		○ Commercial registry entry (https://ag.chregister.ch/cr-portal/auszug/auszug.xhtml?uid=CHE-329.638.515)  currently lists Chris (president, Kollektivunterschrift zu zweien), Tomás (vice president), and Karin (board member, Kollektivunterschrift zu zweien).
	• Karin's understanding of this, but not sure if legally correct:
		○ Currently, only Chris and Karin are allowed to sign contracts for DdS (always in combination).
		○ The board can decide in a board meeting to give Vollmachten to other board members and Xiaojin. The Vollmacht can be open or include details, i.e. on type of contracts of financial cap.
	• Goals of this meeting:
		○ Give a Vollmacht to another board member to sign Greengrocer
		○ Give a Vollmacht to Xiaojin to sign small contracts
		○ Also decide on change in commercial registry to add Xiaojin? --> Decision: take this to another board meeting.


	• Formal vote:
		○ Do you agree that all board members are allowed to sign contracts according to the statutes? All board members agreed.
		○ Do you agree that our director Xiaojin Zhang can sign contracts in operational contracts up to 20k? All board members agreed. 
	• DdS statutes and operational legal aspects need to be checked, so that we can operate without being blocked by aspects in the statutes which once made sense but now have to grow with DdS. 
		
	• Do we agree to add Xiaojin to the commercial registry as CEO --> Taken to the next board meeting. 
	
	• Action items:
		○ Set up Vollmacht documents as voted (Xiaojin), and sign them (Chris&Karin)
		○ Manuel to sign Greengrocer contract
		○ Xiaojin: collect open aspects regarding statutes and legal aspects which arise now with DdS growth. Make sure to adopt a long-term perspective. 
		○ Xiaojin: Make sure our legal understanding of the situation as described above is correct, and the Vollmachten are legally correct. 
